  "summary": "Done. Reading taken: the Details-tab fix is about `GET /api/v1/contracts/{contractId}` returning the field names the page actually reads, so I extended the existing `ContractResponse` additively rather than introducing a second detail DTO.\n\n- `app/schemas/contract.py` — added `contractId`, `lastModified`, `folderTags` (`FolderTagOptionResponse[]`) and `availableTabs` to `ContractResponse`. `id`, `contractName`, `contractType`, `counterpartyName`, `status`, `contractValue`, `currency`, `startDate`, `endDate`, `contractOwnerName` were already spelled exactly as the contract requires, so they were left alone.\n- `app/services/contracts.py` — populates them: `contractId`/`lastModified` from the contract row, `folderTags` via the existing `contract_lifecycle` repo, and `availableTabs` from status using the exact labels `Details, Document, Versions, Clauses, Approvals, Signatures, Obligations, Activity Log`.\n- `tests/test_contracts.py` — one test asserting the detail payload carries these fields.\n\nThe already-existing `/versions`, `/activity-log`, `/document` and `POST /folder-tags` endpoints already match the contract's spelling (`versionId/versionNumber/createdAt/createdBy/changeSummary`, `entryId/performedBy/performedAt`, the full document DTO, `contractId/folderTags`), so I changed nothing there. Full suite: 539 passed.",
