    "notes": "The detail endpoint now returns contractId, lastModified, folderTags and availableTabs in addition to the existing uc123 fields, so the names the UI reads (id, contractType, counterpartyName, contractValue, currency, contractOwnerName) are all present. It does NOT return counterparty, value or owner — the old ContractDetailResponse typedef's spellings do not exist on the wire; use counterpartyName/contractValue/contractOwnerName. availableTabs is built in app/services/contracts.py as Details, Document, Versions, Clauses, then Approvals/Signatures/Obligations when the status warrants, then Activity Log last (a Draft contract gets only the five base labels). /versions and /activity-log return items + page + pageSize + totalCount (not just items/totalCount) and accept page/pageSize query params."
